{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::execute` receives a context for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.source_node` and computes its\ncompleted answer:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse std::future::Future;\n\n// Defined in trust_but_verify::graph.\npub enum ValidationError<E> {\n    Graph(E),\n    NoAgentConfigured,\n    Agent(String),\n    Output(serde_json::Error),\n}\n\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Select inputs through cx and compute the completed answer.\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        cx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nAn `Ok` value is the answer defined by\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.criterion_trait.answer`.\nAn `Err` value reports an execution error.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged this from the supplied test source alone and did not request implementation source. The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.validation.execute`.\n\nThe requirement has three testable parts. `execute` receives a context for the criterion's source node. An `Ok` value is the completed answer. An `Err` value is an execution error of one of four kinds: `Graph`, `NoAgentConfigured`, `Agent(String)` or `Output(serde_json::Error)`. The exact signature is a compile-time shape, and every test that implements or calls `Criterion::execute` enforces it.\n\n**Source-node context and `Ok` answers**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]` runs a criterion through `verify` without an agent. It asserts the computed output and rationale. It also asserts that the recorded dependency is `Dependency::Node(Node(1), …)` for the source node's contents.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync]` verifies `Review` criteria and checks the returned outputs (17 and 23). It also checks that the answers survive store and load.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[criterion_decode_errors_are_execution_errors_and_false_is_a_completed_answer]` shows that a negative result (`false`) is an `Ok` completed answer. It checks the answer's dependencies and the stored JSON.\n- `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]` checks a negative `Ok` answer from a real SDK criterion.\n\n**`Err` variants as execution errors**\n- `Graph(E)`: `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments]` has a node read fail inside the criterion callback. `verify` returns `Err(Graph(\"missing\"))` and nothing is stored.\n- `NoAgentConfigured`: `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` calls `verify` on a criterion that asks the agent while none is configured. It asserts `Err(NoAgentConfigured)` and that no records were stored. It then adds an agent and gets `Ok`.\n- `Agent(String)`: `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error]` makes the agent return an invalid submission. Both `ctx.ask` and `verify` return `Err(Agent(_))`, and nothing is stored. `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload]` checks that the payload is a `String`.\n- `Output(serde_json::Error)`: the decode-error test in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs` returns `ValidationError::Output` when the criterion parses invalid JSON. It asserts the error is a syntax error and that no record was stored.\n\nEach obligation has a scenario with an assertion on its outcome. I found no uncovered obligation, so no gaps or acknowledgments apply.",
